{
  "result": "Okay. Not a task, then. Just thinking out loud.\n\nIf I could change the world in one way, I'd give everyone the ability to, for just a minute, truly feel what another person is feeling \u2014 not imagine it, not sympathize from a distance, but actually experience their fear, their shame, their hope, exactly as they do.\n\nNot forever. That would be overwhelming. Just long enough that it becomes impossible to pretend the other person isn't real in the same way you are.\n\nI don't think it would end disagreement. People would still want different things, believe different things, make selfish choices sometimes. But I think it would end dehumanization, which is where so much cruelty starts. It's much harder to dismiss, humiliate, or hurt someone once you've briefly *been* them.\n\nSo much of the world seems to break down not from a lack of information, but from a failure to really register each other. I'd fix that.",
